# PEEK - Inspect memory in hexadecimal

```text
PEEK first [last]
```

PEEK shows memory bytes and their ASCII equivalents. Both addresses are
hexadecimal. With one address it displays 256 bytes. Two addresses
select an inclusive range. P is the short command name.

```text
GET D0:TEST.COM
PEEK 0100 011F
```

Use [DUMP](DUMP.HLP) to inspect bytes on disk without loading a program
image.
